    {
      "claim_id": "sql_no_prefix/Q1.5/039",
      "text": "1. **Excellent agreement across methods.** All three independent techniques converge on **η ≈ 1.08 mPa·s** for pure liquid ethanol at 25 °C and atmospheric pressure. This is consistent with the widely accepted literature value of **1.074–1.083 mPa·s**.",
      "line": 101,
      "category": "domain_knowledge",
      "incorrect": false,
      "reason": "Reasonable rounded comparison; ordinary 92.3–101.8 kPa laboratory pressures are practical ambient.",
      "evidence": [
        "https://www.nist.gov/publications/reference-correlation-viscosity-ethanol-triple-point-620-k-and-102-mpa",
        "evidence/reference_viscosity_table_audit.json"
      ]
    },
    {
